{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>Do not turn.</b> A warning against the master of an ov and a yide'oni; a master of an ov — this is the python that speaks from its armpit, and a yide'oni — one who inserts a bone of a living creature called yadu'a into his mouth, and the bone speaks (Sanhedrin 65)." "<b>Do not seek.</b> To be occupied with them — for if you occupy yourselves with them, you become defiled before Me and I detest you." "<b>I am YHWH your Elohim.</b> Know Whom you are exchanging for what (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:18.913174349Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}